From: king-nRXb03v5zC6Vc3sceRu5cw at public.gmane.org (Gary King)
Date: Thu, 20 May 2010 15:31:35 -0400
Subject: Re: mlogit
In-Reply-To: <32FC35943F9EE94ABFEFAEA6FE7C7CE8107664@whitney.ppic.org>
References: <32FC35943F9EE94ABFEFAEA6FE7C7CE8107660@whitney.ppic.org> <AANLkTilloy6_vAMgBTba3IoK3MzEMn0kTedgc6Hjp-ew@mail.gmail.com> <32FC35943F9EE94ABFEFAEA6FE7C7CE8107664@whitney.ppic.org>
Message-ID: <AANLkTikvCQ69DOGxC_b7XEBjaoeounyi_rJuFFbRS6eh@mail.gmail.com>

its probably collinearity.  run a regression; if that works (with all
the variables included), the mlogit will usually work.

stats runs anything but it does that by dropping variables.  so unless
you're watching closely, you wind up estimating a model you didn't ask
it to run.

Gary
